# docs/KEYMAP.md §Workspace prefix — `^s a` starts a native Claude thread in this worktree
# docs/KEYMAP.md §Native agent thread — `Agent > AgentIdle` ⇄ `Agent > AgentWorking`
# docs/NATIVE-AGENTS.md §3.3 — the attention vocabulary a row and a tab mark carry
# docs/TESTING-HARNESS.md §5 — the scripted `two-turns.json` the `agents` preset gives Claude
#
# One streaming turn, start to finish: the thread is created, streams, settles, and says so.
fixture: agents
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000
assert mode == Terminal && lists.tabs.rows[3] absent

# A native tab joins the process tabs in one numbering, and carries its provider as a badge.
key ctrl-s a
await agents.threads[0].provider == claude 20000
assert mode == Agent && key_contexts[0] == Agent && key_contexts[1] == AgentIdle
assert lists.tabs.selected.badges[0] == claude && lists.tabs.selected.label == Claude && focused == agents.composer
await idle 30000
type what does this crate do
key enter

# The turn streams: the derived context follows daemon state, and the tab mark follows with it.
await agents.threads[0].state == working 20000
assert key_contexts[1] == AgentWorking && lists.tabs.selected.marks[0] == working
shot streaming
dump streaming

# `end_turn` is the transcript's turn terminal; Fleet settles the thread and toasts once.
await agents.threads[0].state == idle 40000
assert key_contexts[1] == AgentIdle && agents.threads[0].pending_gate absent
assert lists.tabs.selected.marks[0] == idle && lists.tabs.selected.label == "what does this crate do"
assert toasts[0].level == warning && toasts[0].text ~= "agent finished"
dump finished
quit
